    "title": "Blue Ridge Artisan Days Fall Festival returns to Gray this weekend - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Faith Little Brody Wilson ,\n10 hours ago\nGRAY, Tenn. (WJHL) - Shoppers looking for handmade goods, seasonal decorations, and unique gifts will have a chance to support local businesses this weekend at the Blue Ridge Artisan Days Fall Festival.\nThe two-day event will take place at the Appalachian Fairgrounds on Friday, Oct. 23, from 3:00-7:00 p.m. and Saturday, Oct. 24, from 9 a.m.- 3 p.m.\nThe festival brings together regional artisans and small businesses offering handcrafted goods, home decor, gifts, specialty foods, and apparel.\nFriday's festivities will also include a costume parade at 6:00 p.m.\nMore information can be found here .\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WJHL | Tri-Cities News & Weather.",
    "summary": "By Faith Little Brody Wilson , GRAY, Tenn. (WJHL) - Shoppers looking for handmade goods, seasonal decorations, and unique gifts will have a chance to support local businesses this weekend at the Blue Ridge Artisan Days Fall Festival. The two-day event will take place at the Appalachian Fairgrounds on Friday, Oct. 23, from 3:00-7:00 p.m. and Saturday, Oct. 24, from 9 a.m.- 3 p.m. The festival brings together regional artisans and small businesses offering handcrafted goods, home decor, gifts, specialty foods, and apparel.",
